From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: ntdll, kernelbase: a packaged process's package graph

A packaged application loads DLLs from the frameworks it depends on (the
Visual C++ runtime's _app DLLs, the Windows App SDK). At process start,
before imports are resolved, ntdll finds the package whose install
location holds the executable (appxdeploymentclient's records) and puts
its Dependencies' install locations at the front of PATH. Processes
outside a package only pay an unsuccessful registry open.

GetCurrentPackageInfo (was a stub) returns the same graph: the package
(PACKAGE_FILTER_HEAD) and its frameworks (PACKAGE_FILTER_DIRECT,
PACKAGE_PROPERTY_FRAMEWORK), with paths, names and package IDs. appmodel.h
gains PACKAGE_INFO and the PACKAGE_FILTER/PROPERTY/INFORMATION values.

